{%- comment -%}
  Cellexia Reviews — single source of the storefront app-proxy base path.

  v1.6.0 (SPEC-1.6 §2): the value is now METAFIELD-DRIVEN. The app probes the
  live storefront (`probeProxySubpath`) and writes the subpath it proved working
  into the SHOP metafield `cellexia.proxy_path` (single_line_text_field, e.g.
  "cellexia-reviews"). Liquid renders that value, so the theme extension can no
  longer drift from the [app_proxy] block in shopify.app.toml — whatever subpath
  the merchant's app is actually mounted on is what the storefront calls.

  Nil-safe: an absent metafield, an empty value or a whitespace-only value falls
  back to the default subpath "cellexia-reviews". Stray slashes and spaces are
  stripped so a value pasted as "/apps/cellexia-reviews/" still yields a single
  clean path segment.

  Consumers: blocks/reviews.liquid + blocks/embed.liquid render it into
  data-proxy, and embed.liquid also carries it in the #cx-embed-config JSON
  (badge-only pages have no widget root to read the attribute from). If even
  this value is wrong, assets/cellexia-reviews.js runs ONE client-side discovery
  sweep over the known candidate subpaths and retries — see SPEC-1.6 §2.

  Output contract: exactly "/apps/<subpath>/api", no surrounding whitespace.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign cx_proxy_subpath = shop.metafields.cellexia.proxy_path.value | default: '' | append: '' | strip
  assign cx_proxy_subpath = cx_proxy_subpath | remove: '/' | remove: ' '
  if cx_proxy_subpath == blank
    assign cx_proxy_subpath = 'cellexia-reviews'
  endif
-%}
{{- '/apps/' | append: cx_proxy_subpath | append: '/api' -}}
